# Docs sync, style and VM-only runs

- Run browsers, the app and tests only on the test VM via `npm run vm:*` (docs/vm.md). Never on the developer Mac; do not install browsers or project dependencies there. `npm run lint` is the only thing that runs on the Mac.
- Docs mirror the code path: `src/a/b.js` is documented in `docs/src/a/b.js.md`.
- Before editing a code file, read its mirrored doc. After editing, fix stale parts and add missing information in the same commit.
- New code file needs a new doc. Deleted code file needs its doc deleted.
- Code style: minimal and readable. Multi-line comments only at the top of a file. Explanations belong in `docs/`.
- Scratch files go in `<repo>/tmp/` (never `/tmp`); delete them when done, with the Delete tool.
- Behavior changes also need `npm run vm:verify` to pass (see `docs/visual.md`).
- Run `npm run lint` and `npm run vm:test` before committing.

Full rules: `AGENTS.md` and `docs/guidelines.md`.
